From 639f55f9fb5539cfefad4598642ffce13bc3dcc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniket Singh Yadav <singhyadavaniket43@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:43:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Downsample thumbnails in numpy instead of importing
 scipy.ndimage

Image and Labels thumbnails used scipy.ndimage.zoom with order=0, a pure
nearest-neighbour lookup. The import of scipy.ndimage (about 200 modules,
scipy.special among them) was the largest cost of the first image after
xarray, and the zoom ran again on every slice. zoom_nearest in
layer_utils returns the same pixels; the one difference is that where
floating-point error put the last coordinate a hair past the last pixel,
scipy's default mode blanked that row or column, and the edge pixel is
used instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/napari/layers/image/image.py       | 13 ++++---------
 src/napari/layers/labels/labels.py     |  5 ++---
 src/napari/layers/utils/layer_utils.py | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

